oesn't develop pieces.\n\nReason:\nI choose **N: g8-f6** because:\n- It develops a piece toward the center following classical opening principles\n- It attacks White's advanced e4 pawn immediately\n- It prepares kingside castling (after developing the f8 bishop)\n- The knight on f6 is optimally placed for both attack and defense\n- This is the most natural and flexible move, maintaining maximum options for future play\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
