 tactical opportunity.\n\n5. **N: g3-h5** - Attacks the queen on g4 but allows it to move while maintaining pressure.\n\nReason: N: g3-f1 is the strongest move. It gives check to the White king on e1, forcing an immediate response. Since White's king hasn't castled and is stuck in the center, this check is particularly powerful. The knight on f1 would be protected and would completely disrupt White's coordination. This forcing move maintains my initiative and exploits White's vulnerable king position.\n\nAnswer: N: g3-f1"}
