tive. With White's King exposed and unable to castle, this check could lead to a strong attack.\n\nReason:\nGiving check with Qh4+ exploits White's biggest weakness - the uncastled King on e1. This forcing move seizes the initiative, prevents White from coordinating their pieces smoothly, and potentially allows me to launch a kingside attack. The Queen on h4 would be actively placed, eyeing both the King and potentially supporting further aggressive moves.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
