ively.\n\nReason: I choose **N: b8-c6** because:\n- It develops a piece that hasn't moved yet\n- The knight on c6 controls key central squares\n- It prepares for further piece coordination (potentially allowing d7-d5 later with the knight supporting)\n- It's a solid, principled move that improves my position without creating weaknesses\n- Development is crucial, and getting pieces into the game is a high priority\n\nAnswer: N: b8-c6"}
