n you have a forcing move like check, especially one that improves your piece position, it's usually the best choice. This move:\n- Forces White's king to move (likely Kf1, Ke1, Kg1, Kf3, or Kg3)\n- Centralizes my knight even further\n- Disrupts White's coordination\n- May create follow-up tactical opportunities depending on where the king moves\n\nAnswer: N: d4-e2"}
