aining protection of anything critical, White will be forced into a passive position. This move forces White's hand immediately and maintains maximum pressure. After White's rook moves, I can potentially push my queenside pawns or reposition my pieces for a winning attack. The immediate tactical pressure is more valuable than slowly improving my position.\n\nAnswer: R: f1-a1"}
