5-e4** is the strongest move because:\n- It attacks White's f3 pawn, threatening to capture it\n- It controls key central squares (d3, c2, d5 access routes)\n- It maintains active piece play\n- After capturing on f3 (if allowed), I'd have an overwhelming material advantage\n- It prevents White's king from easily supporting the f3 pawn's advance\n\nAnswer: B: f5-e4"}
