 check to the White king on e5, forcing it to move to a worse square (likely d4, d5, e6, or f5). This disrupts White's king activity and allows me to improve my position. After forcing the king back, I can activate my own king and coordinate my pieces better to convert my material advantage. The check is a forcing move that improves my position while worsening White's.\n\nAnswer: P: f7-f6"}
